 The startup block (format 2, `startupBlock`) is built with reads only, in one transaction. Essentials gathers the active pinned memories of the personal notebook (`shared`; a project memory on the same topic hides the shared one), of the group's board (the `ecosystem/estado-actual` status note first) and of the project, in that order, and within each newest first. The index gathers the titles of the active unpinned memories of the board and the project, alternating one from the board and one from the project so that neither drawer crowds out the other; it leaves out session summaries and the unpinned personal notebook. With schema 11, superseded memories are also left out, the short version replaces the title in essentials, the `[verify]` mark appears, and the previous interrupted session is included. The limits (5,000 in total, 1,500 for essentials, 800 for the previous session) are counted in Unicode characters; each list is filled in order and stops at the first line that does not fit, and what is left out is added up in `omitted`. The widest possible header is reserved before filling, and the final header prints the block's exact occupancy (`<chars>/5000 chars`).
 
-PostgreSQL synchronization transfers a versioned snapshot of local state. It is optional, explicit, and cannot replace the local SQLite/FTS5 read/write path. Format promotion requires `sync --upgrade-format` after every participating device is compatible. `ecosystem` memories are not replicated yet: until format 4 (its own plan, 1.8.0), `sync` stops with `SYNC_ECOSYSTEM_UNSUPPORTED` if they exist.
+PostgreSQL synchronization transfers a versioned snapshot of local state. It is optional, explicit, and cannot replace the local SQLite/FTS5 read/write path. Format promotion requires `sync --upgrade-format` after every participating device is compatible. A new database (schema 11) already uses format 3, so its first `sync` against a replica in an earlier format, including a freshly created one, stops with `SYNC_UPGRADE_REQUIRED` until `sync --upgrade-format` is used. `ecosystem` memories are not replicated yet: until format 4 (its own plan, 1.8.0), `sync` stops with `SYNC_ECOSYSTEM_UNSUPPORTED` if they exist.
 
 The product currently ships verified macOS and Linux standalone binaries. There is no Windows native addon, installer, or release artifact in the current product.
